  "views": {
    "hero": "top",
    "reads": {
      "front": "A towering bolt from the top of frame, thick and forked, with a second strand twisting around it. The warning ring, shockwave and scorch are thin bright lines on the ground, so the bolt and screen flash carry this view.",
      "side": "Same column edge-on with a different branch pattern; checks the bolt and its strands have depth. The shockwave reads as a flat line expanding left and right.",
      "top": "Hero view. The bolt is a blinding point, so the ground tells the story: a wide static-filled warning ring that tightens during the charge, then a big shockwave ring, sparks spraying out radially and a large cracked scorch that lingers. The charge telegraph is a pulsing warning circle on the ground that shrinks onto the strike zone; the strike leaves a crater with glowing cracks that cool, and the crater stays after the spell.",
      "three_quarter": "Bolt reads tall and heavy, and the warning ring, shockwave and scorch read as wide ellipses, so you see both the strike and how much ground it covers."
    }
